cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HypGraph in your research or teaching, please cite it."
title: "HypGraph: a research record that can't flatter itself"
abstract: >-
  An append-only, hash-chained record of questions, hypotheses, experiments, runs, results, claims, sources,
  reviews and decisions, whose standing (review, risk, independent support, evidence strength) is derived on read
  and never asserted. Claims are checked on write: numbers bound to results, absolutes backed by k of n, exclusions
  backed by a powered search.
type: software
authors:
